{"id": "xgreenland", "name": "Northeast Greenland National Park", "short": "NE Greenland", "place": "Greenland", "lat": 77.0, "lon": -23.0, "side": "r", "cont": "North America", "country": "Greenland", "kind": "Polar & mountain", "park": true, "blurb": "Muskoxen, lemmings and polar bears on tundra and sea ice.", "tip": {"id": "seaice", "title": "Lose the sea ice", "text": "Sea ice carries ice algae, copepods, polar cod and seals. Set Sea ice to -100% and watch the polar bear and the foxes that scavenge its kills."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Northeast Greenland National Park", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northeast_Greenland_National_Park"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Muskox", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muskox"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Arctic fox", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arctic_fox"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Polar bear", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polar_bear"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Northeast Greenland National Park", "icon": "ice", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "salix", "sp": "salix arctica", "xh": 0.1}, {"id": "dryas", "sp": "dryas octopetala", "xh": 0.28}, {"id": "carex", "sp": "carex", "xh": 0.46, "desc": "Grass-like plants of wet tundra. Muskoxen and barnacle geese graze sedges and grasses."}, {"id": "cassiope", "sp": "cassiope tetragona", "xh": 0.64}, {"id": "icealgae", "sp": "bacillariophyceae", "xh": 0.85, "name": "Sea-ice algae", "wiki": "Ice algae", "desc": "Microscopic algae that grow in and under sea ice, the base of the marine food chain here."}, {"id": "muskox", "sp": "ovibos moschatus", "xh": 0.08, "desc": "The park holds a large share of the world population. It eats grasses, sedges and willows, and Arctic wolves are its main predator.", "badge": "Keystone grazer"}, {"id": "lemming", "sp": "dicrostonyx groenlandicus", "xh": 0.26, "desc": "A small tundra rodent that turns white in winter. Its numbers rise and fall in cycles, which drive its predators."}, {"id": "hare", "sp": "lepus arcticus", "xh": 0.44}, {"id": "goose", "sp": "branta leucopsis", "xh": 0.62, "desc": "A summer breeding visitor that grazes sedges and grasses. It is one of the most recorded birds here.", "ic": "hawk"}, {"id": "calanus", "sp": "calanus glacialis", "xh": 0.85, "name": "Arctic copepod", "desc": "A tiny crustacean of Arctic seas that feeds on ice algae and phytoplankton and feeds fish.", "ic": "hopper"}, {"id": "fox", "sp": "vulpes lagopus", "xh": 0.08, "desc": "Hunts lemmings, hares and birds, and scavenges carcasses left by polar bears and wolves."}, {"id": "stoat", "sp": "mustela erminea", "xh": 0.22, "desc": "A small weasel listed among the park's land mammals. It preys on lemmings and other small animals."}, {"id": "jaeger", "sp": "stercorarius longicaudus", "xh": 0.36}, {"id": "raven", "sp": "corvus corax", "xh": 0.5, "desc": "A year-round resident that scavenges carcasses and other leftovers."}, {"id": "cod", "sp": "boreogadus saida", "xh": 0.72, "name": "Polar cod", "wiki": "Polar cod", "desc": "A small fish living near sea ice that feeds on copepods and is prey for seals."}, {"id": "ringed", "sp": "pusa hispida", "xh": 0.88, "desc": "The most common prey of polar bears, and a seal that depends on sea ice. It eats fish and crustaceans."}, {"id": "wolf", "sp": "canis lupus", "xh": 0.25, "name": "Arctic wolf", "wiki": "Arctic wolf", "desc": "A small but important population lives here. Wolves are the main predator of muskoxen and also take hares and birds."}, {"id": "bear", "sp": "ursus maritimus", "xh": 0.75, "desc": "Hunts mainly ringed seals from the sea ice. Its kills feed foxes and ravens."}, {"id": "sun", "sp": "midnight sun", "xh": 0.1}, {"id": "soil", "sp": "tundra soil", "xh": 0.35}, {"id": "decomp", "sp": "decomposers",